  "scenario": {
    "summary": "Guest opens the Departments menu, checks the listed top-level categories, then hovers five parent categories (Hardware, Lawn Care, Plumbing, Tools, HVAC) and checks each sub-category list.",
    "steps": [
      "Open the webstore, open the Departments menu",
      "Verify the category list against the sheet table",
      "Hover each of five parent categories from the sheet",
      "Verify each parent's sub-category names against its sheet table"
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "category"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "None"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "Departments list equals the sheet table",
      "Each hovered parent's sub-categories equal its sheet table"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "Not scanned: categoriesMap, categoryWithSubCategoryMap (5 parent names) and the five sub-category tables (hardware/lawnCare/plumbing/tools/hvac) are whole sheet tables read with TestData.getHashMap; the scan only records the map keys categoryWithSubCategories0..4 (literals, config).",
      "departments = CATEGORIES_TOP_LEVEL_OF_STORE {store, minCategories 8}: the Departments menu in display order (category1Name..category8Name); same param set as the approved Playwright plp entry. The migrated method compares the menu with these outputs instead of the sheet table.",
      "category = CATEGORY_WITH_PRODUCTS {store, minProducts 1, topLevel true, minSubcategories 4}: a top-level category with at least 4 active sub-categories; hover category.name and check subcategory1Name..subcategory4Name are in the fly-out (the key returns at most 4; same approach as the plp verifyCategoryHeadingAndListedSubCategories decision 2026-11-10). This replaces the five hard-coded parents with one resolved parent (the key has no 'not this category' param, so five needs would resolve the same record); accepted by the user 2026-11-11.",
      "Store: openWebstoreUrl opens automation_webStoreUrl (atstage: webstore-z10-atstage, the main store MaxwellsHardware), the same store as the Selenium pdp/quickOrder/plp entries.",
      "Profile: work/profiles/profile.json has no observations for these Selenium cells (profiled false); DB facts from bin/tda rows (2026-11-11) where cited.",
      "Scanned constant values (locators, report messages, map keys, image paths) are framework constants: role config, no need.",
      "migrate: Selenium reads Excel tables through TestData.getMap / getHashMap; there is no swap for Selenium."
    ],
    "confidence": "medium",
    "needsReview": false
  },
